From 141152501c55cef98be3f0d74c6068ca6ea94597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vladimir Oltean <vladimir.oltean@nxp.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 16:53:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 46/48] phy: lynx: disable RX_HAPPY module for KR link training

It was observed on 25GBase-KR, with some short channesl that when the
link partner starts with coefficient sets which are compliant to IEEE
requirements for INIT (Rpre, Rpst), the RX_HAPPY module complains and
requests a jump to PRESET coefficients.

More investigation regarding the RX_HAPPY module is necessary. Until
then, bypass the condition and allow just the BinLong/BinM1 modules to
do the work.

Signed-off-by: Vladimir Oltean <vladimir.oltean@nxp.com>
---
 drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-xgkr-algorithm.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-xgkr-algorithm.c b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-xgkr-algorithm.c
index e52c6bb82c50..74d52302cbf3 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-xgkr-algorithm.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/freescale/phy-fsl-lynx-xgkr-algorithm.c
@@ -542,6 +542,7 @@ lynx_xgkr_train_remote_tx(struct lynx_xgkr_algorithm *algorithm,
 		return lynx_xgkr_remote_tx_request(rts, UPDATE_REQUESTER_INIT);
 	}
 
+#if 0
 	for (i = 0; i < TIMEOUT_RX_HAPPY; i++) {
 		is_rx_happy = lynx_xgkr_is_rx_happy(algorithm);
 		if (is_rx_happy)
@@ -551,6 +552,7 @@ lynx_xgkr_train_remote_tx(struct lynx_xgkr_algorithm *algorithm,
 	if (!is_rx_happy)
 		return lynx_xgkr_process_bad_state(algorithm, remote_tx,
 						   BAD_STATE_RX_NOT_HAPPY);
+#endif
 
 	/* Move to BinLong/BinM1 modules */
 
